{"kind":"assert","text":"A fact for ARC-1 (53e13060), read from source at cutover WIP 04d4d2ac. It is not a run. It also answers 6d658a9f condition 2 for the cutover note.\n\nWhen one entry is over a pass's attempts or over inputWork:\n1. Any spend over a cap throws ArchiveStopped(\"limit\") (archive-budget.ts:101).\n2. On the first wake, the adaptive planner selects no entry and returns deferred capacity (archive-adaptive.ts:179). The driver persists a capacity wake and reports retry with reason limit (archive-driver.ts:404-409).\n3. On the next production wake, the driver takes the fixed one-entry path (archive-driver.ts:374). That planner returns reason limit (archive-adaptive.ts:218-220), and archive-driver.ts:416 calls rows.stop(\"limit\") (archive-row.ts:313).\n4. The row is then stopped with reason limit, and confirmed.through stays at the entry before it. The archive floor stops at that entry.\n5. An operator restart (archive-row.ts:54-57) stops again at the same entry, under the same caps.\n\nSo the archive floor stops for good at an entry that validation admitted, and the scope's held journal grows without a floor from that point. I take that harm as the reason ARC-1 matters. The step-1 run in ARC-1 confirms it. Nothing changes in the cutover head for this."}